# Your Design Rules

If the `your-design-rules` skill is installed, follow its SKILL.md. Otherwise use the rule files copied into
`design-rules/` at the project root:

1. Read `design-rules/rules/core.md` first.
2. Read the guide for the task in `design-rules/guides/` (web-app, landing-page, mobile-app,
   dashboard-and-tables, slides).
3. No brand or style given? Pick one archetype from `design-rules/archetypes/README.md`, say which and why,
   and read its file. User-specified fonts and colors always win.
4. Consult `design-rules/rules/layout.md`, `typography.md`, `color.md`, `imagery-and-icons.md`, `motion.md` as needed.
5. Build section by section; after each section render it and run `design-rules/rules/review-checklist.md`.
   Fix in place.

Non-negotiables:
- One job, one primary action, one dominant region per view.
- No card-wrapping without a job; separate with whitespace, alignment, hairlines, or tone.
- Gradients, shadows, big radii, glow, glass only on purpose; shadows soft and diffuse, never hard.
- No beige, cream, ivory, tan, or warm off-white backgrounds.
- Accent color only for actions and selection.
- No invented metrics, logos, testimonials, or image URLs; label samples as samples.
- Build UI from real elements, never images of UI; never hand-draw logos from SVG paths.
- Motion only with a job: 150–350 ms, ease-out curves, transform and opacity only, respect reduced motion.
- Body text ≥ 16 px on web, contrast ≥ 4.5:1, tap targets ≥ 44 px.
